    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-03",
      "edition": "Tuesday 3 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Leinster appointment",
          "heading": "Ireland great Cian Healy rejoins Leinster as full-time player development officer",
          "body": "Healy has taken a full-time post with Leinster, working with the province's most promising young players as an elite player development officer. He started the job last month after coaching with Clontarf in the All-Ireland League and Belvedere College since retiring in 2025. He filled in on Leinster's matchday coaching staff for last weekend's URC win over Connacht, covering for Seán O'Brien, who was on leave after the birth of his daughter. Leo Cullen's verdict: \"Cian is in the building with us now, which is fantastic.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England call up Spencer and Randall; Mitchell, McParland out",
