    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-03",
      "edition": "Tuesday 3 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Townsend loses Ritchie and Millar Mills, calls up uncapped Blyth-Lafferty",
          "body": "Scotland's New Zealand build-up has lost two forwards from the extended squad. Jamie Ritchie, who joined Glasgow from Perpignan this summer, came off early in Glasgow's win over the Lions with an injury, while Newcastle prop Elliot Millar Mills went off after minutes of Newcastle's defeat. Replacing them are uncapped Edinburgh prop Ollie Blyth-Lafferty, fellow Edinburgh prop D'Arcy Rae and Edinburgh back-rower Freddy Douglas, with Sale scrum-half Gus Warr also training this week."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England call up Spencer and Randall; Mitchell, McParland out",
