      "edition": "Tuesday 3 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Legal threat",
          "heading": "URC threatens WRU with legal action over Premiership talks for Welsh clubs",
          "body": "WalesOnline understands the URC has written to the WRU telling it not to enter formal discussions with the RFU or Premiership Rugby, and has threatened legal action if those talks continue. The competition insists Wales keep four sides, and the WRU, an equal shareholder, is contractually obliged to supply them. Abi Tierney confirmed the English talks at a Professional Rugby Board meeting last week, and the Ospreys and Scarlets remain in the firing line over the three-team plan."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England call up Spencer and Randall; Mitchell, McParland out",
