      "edition": "Tuesday 3 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Les Kiss explains Pietsch omission as Wallabies turn to experience",
          "body": "Les Kiss has gone into the reasons for leaving Pietsch out and the fullback contest that follows. The clearest sign of the experience push is Kurtley Beale, 37, named in the touring party after five years away from international rugby and added once Hunter Paisami made himself unavailable for personal reasons. \"No one comes in just to fill a void,\" Kiss said, placing Beale at 12 with the chance to flex to 15 and 10. Former All Black Jeff Wilson has called the move backwards."
        },
